 in news lisa there's been a new  arrest in this case what can you tell us  about that  well police just confirmed me that they  indeed  arrested a 47 year old man apparently  that man  was living in the region around nice  and he is originally from a maghrib  country now he was on the phone with the  attacker  several times the day before the attack  so two days ago  and the police are now looking into the  question if  he was just in touch or if he was an  accomplice  of the murderer the the assailant who  killed three people  at the cathedral just behind me if  france is at its highest  terror alert level what does that  actually mean  well it means that an additional 4 000  soldiers and police forces are deployed  across the country at them  are being deployed across the country at  the moment to protect  vulnerable locations here in france  the police told me that they considered  that  under the lockdown because france has  now entered a lockdown for  probably at least four weeks under the  lockdown  vulnerable places are not only places of  worship and those  locations where terror attacks happened  in the past  but also public transport because under  the lockdown that's where people are  crowded really  so the polices really are really on high  alert and they're trying to protect as  many places as they can at the moment  well today lisa france is going into  lockdown um how will that affect the  both the um the public commemoration  uh of these latest killings and and also  the investigation  well obviously you know public  commemorations will be difficult to  carry out if you look back a few weeks  you know when samuel patti was beheaded  by a  a radical islamist the teacher who had  shown a cartoon of the prophet of  muhammad  in his classroom after that president  he indeed held a public ceremony to  commemorate  this man but this will hardly be  possible now here in france under  lockdown there might be some online  event or something or  email mccomb 