 they get support out of tunisia did  he have any support in italy  that'll be important but what we've seen  certainly in recent cases is that  even if the actor does look to have  acted alone in fact there is a certain  degree of support  online or offline and it could be  international  as you're indicating why is france  seeing  so many islamist terror attacks right  now three over the last two months  well the the overall polarized situation  in france  beginning with the the trial around  charlie abdul the republication of the  caricatures  mid-september uh macon's reactions  uh to to these caricatures uh there  there's  within the muslim community there's some  that are denouncing this but in  extremist circles this is used again as  proof that france must be targeted the  calls for  attacks uh against french institutions  french symbols  in france and outside of france as we  signed jeddah yesterday as well  have been made so right now france has  become through the  the free speech debate and the challenge  situation  a major focal point again for extremist  circles  and this is probably inciting the recent  attacks  the lockdown conditions in the country  right now do they make  terrorist attacks easier and and how do  they affect the police investigation  well the the police investigation isn't  the investigation  per se is not that much affected however  where  it does limit the resources that can be  deployed on the streets and it also  limits the resources  in terms of intelligence gathering  information gathering so  these create issues however right now  with the lockdown  it does reduce the possibility of attack  simply by reducing the number of targets  but as we saw in march  late march this year it doesn't prevent  attacks per se but the probability of  having an attack  is reduced simply by the reducing the  number of targets yon san pierre  counterterrorism advisor security expert  mosicon here in berlin thanks so very  much for those insights 